  "answer": "A shunt generator has a field winding connected in parallel with the external circuit [1]. Because the field winding is connected in parallel to the load and armature, all current flowing in the external circuit passes only through the armature winding, not the field [1]. The output voltage of a shunt generator can be controlled by inserting a rheostat in series with the field windings [1]. As shown in Figure 4-22, the generator includes components such as the field rheostat, field winding, armature winding, shunt circuit, main circuit, and load [1].",
